## Why This Is Asked

This question tests the ability to design streaming algorithms with bounded memory while computing exact results. It captures a common real-world problem: maintaining aggregate statistics over a sliding or growing dataset without storing all historical values.

## Key Concepts

- **Streaming data structures:** Using heaps to maintain top-K elements efficiently
- **Running sum:** Incremental updates avoid recomputing the sum after each batch
- **Time complexity:** O(log K) per element; batch processing takes O(B log K)
- **Memory usage:** O(K) vs O(N) for the exact method that stores all past values

## Code Example

```javascript
function topKSumStream(valueStream, K) {
  const heap = new MinHeap();
  let sum = 0;

  for (const batch of valueStream) {
    for (const v of batch) {
      if (heap.size() < K) {
        heap.push(v);
        sum += v;
      } else if (heap.size() > 0 && v > heap.peek()) {
        sum += v - heap.pop();
        heap.push(v);
      }
    }
    console.log("Top-K sum:", sum);
  }
}
```

## Asymptotic Analysis

| Metric | Our Solution | Exact Method |
|--------|--------------|--------------|
| Per-element update | O(log K) | O(1) |
| Batch time (size B) | O(B log K) | O(B) |
| Memory | O(K) | O(N) |

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to extend classic shortest-paths to dynamic updates with a concrete, real-world constraint (only decreases) and to analyze practical performance in terms of amortized work and memory.

## Key Concepts

- Dynamic single-source shortest paths with only edge decreases
- Amortized analysis and potential-based arguments
- Priority-queue relaxation propagation
- Memory-time trade-offs and localized updates
- Practical optimizations: skip non-on-SPT edges, batch updates, integer weights with Dial's algorithm

## Code Example

```javascript
class DynamicSSSP {
  constructor(graph, source) {
    this.graph = graph; // adjacency: {u: [{v, w}, ...]}
    this.n = Object.keys(graph).length;
    this.dist = Array(this.n).fill(Infinity);
    this.dist[source] = 0;
    this.pq = new MinHeap(); // custom min-heap with push/pop
    this.pq.push([0, source]);
    while (!this.pq.isEmpty()) {
      const [d, u] = this.pq.pop();
      if (d !== this.dist[u]) continue;
      for (const {v, w} of this.graph[u]) {
        if (this.dist[v] > d + w) {
          this.dist[v] = d + w;
          this.pq.push([this.dist[v], v]);
        }
      }
    }
  }
  decreaseEdge(u, v, newW) {
    // update edge weight in graph[u] item
    // assume newW <= oldW
    // attempt relaxation
    if (this.dist[u] + newW < this.dist[v]) {
      this.dist[v] = this.dist[u] + newW;
      this.pq.push([this.dist[v], v]);
      while (!this.pq.isEmpty()) {
        const [d, x] = this.pq.pop();
        if (d !== this.dist[x]) continue;
        for (const {to, w} of this.graph[x] || []) {
          if (this.dist[to] > d + w) {
            this.dist[to] = d + w;
            this.pq.push([this.dist[to], to]);
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

